          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "When drafting wills, **testamentary discretionary trusts (TDTs)**, and **Enduring Powers of Attorney (EPOAs)** under Queensland law, you will want a firm experienced in succession planning and asset protection. Because testamentary trusts involve complex tax considerations and trust succession, choosing a lawyer who handles tailored estate structures rather than just \"simple wills\" is critical.\n\nThe most reputable and established law firms in and immediately adjacent to **Mount Gravatt** and **Sunnybank** include:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Mount Gravatt & Upper Mount Gravatt**\n\n* **Elliott & Harvey Lawyers (Upper Mount Gravatt)**\n  * **Location:** Suite 4, 1953 Logan Road, Upper Mount Gravatt\n  * **Specialty:** Highly regarded for comprehensive estate planning. They routinely draft complex wills, testamentary discretionary trusts, special disability trusts, and handle blended-family arrangements and EPOAs. Their team is experienced in handling both personal estates and multi-entity commercial/family trust succession.\n* **Life Law Solutions (Mount Gravatt East)**\n  * **Location:** 22 Carrara Street, Mount Gravatt East\n  * **Specialty:** A boutique firm specializing strictly in family law, estate planning, and estate administration. They excel at integrating wills, testamentary trusts, Binding Death Benefit Nominations (BDBNs) for superannuation, and Advance Health Directives into a structured, holistic plan.\n* **Bennett Carroll Solicitors (Upper Mount Gravatt)**\n  * **Location:** 2085 Logan Road (near Westfield Mt Gravatt), Upper Mount Gravatt\n  * **Specialty:** A prominent, full-service firm with a dedicated wills and estates practice group. They specialize in asset-protection strategies, testamentary trusts for tax minimization, and setting up EPOAs with clear protective conditions.\n* **Campbells Legal Services (Upper Mount Gravatt)**\n  * **Location:** Upper Mount Gravatt\n  * **Specialty:** Boutique practice focusing heavily on modern Queensland succession law (including changes under Queensland trust legislation), testamentary trusts, capacity issues, and enduring powers of attorney.\n* **Ian W. Bartels & Associates (Mount Gravatt)**\n  * **Location:** 1408 Logan Road, Mount Gravatt\n  * **Specialty:** A long-standing, traditional Southside practice. Great for straightforward estates, EPOAs, and probate administration at transparent rates.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Sunnybank & Sunnybank Hills**\n\n* **Wheldon & Associates (Sunnybank)**\n  * **Location:** 12 Zamia Street, Sunnybank\n  * **Specialty:** One of the most established legal practices in Sunnybank. They have decades of experience drafting wills, establishing testamentary and family trusts, and structuring EPOAs to prevent disputes or financial abuse down the track.\n* **Times Lawyers (Sunnybank)**\n  * **Location:** Mains Road, Sunnybank (near Sunnybank Plaza / Market Square)\n  * **Specialty:** A well-known multilingual firm (English, Mandarin, Cantonese) catering to the diverse local community. Excellent if your estate involves both local and cross-border/overseas assets or if family members require language support during estate planning.\n* **Denovo Lawyers (Sunnybank Hills)**\n  * **Location:** Sunnybank Hills\n  * **Specialty:** A modern boutique firm providing clear, fixed-fee estate planning services, including comprehensive wills, EPOAs, and protective trust mechanisms.\n* **Madsen Law (Sunnybank / Southside)**\n  * **Location:** Sunnybank\n  * **Specialty:** Strong expertise at the intersection of family law and estate planning—vital if you have blended families, adult children with financial vulnerabilities, or concerns about future family provision claims.\n\n---\n\n### **Key Questions to Ask Before Engaging a Lawyer:**\n\n1. **Fixed Fee vs. Hourly:** Most firms offer fixed-fee packages for an \"Estate Planning Pack\" (Will with Testamentary Trust + EPOA + Advance Health Directive). Always ask for a fixed-price quote upfront.\n2. **Control Mechanisms for Testamentary Trusts:** Ask the lawyer how they structure the **Appointor** and **Trustee** roles in the trust deed, especially if you want your beneficiaries to have asset protection against future divorces or bankruptcy.\n3. **Superannuation Integration:** Super does not automatically form part of your will. Ensure the lawyer reviews your superannuation trust deeds and assists with a valid **Binding Death Benefit Nomination (BDBN)**.\n4. **Capacity & Execution:** Under the *Powers of Attorney Act 1998 (Qld)*, strict witnessing and capacity requirements apply when signing an EPOA. Ensure your solicitor arranges the formal witnessing on-site.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
